  "id": "controlled-attention",
  "term": "controlled attention",
  "definition": "Controlled attention is attention that depends on executive control resources to direct focus according to current goals. In this source, temporal orienting is described as needing controlled attention, unlike rhythm-based temporal preparation, which appears to operate without such executive control.",
